cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it."

title: "GEO-Hubble Geometric Projection"
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Torreblanca"
    given-names: "Leonel Hernan"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-2095-4499"

version: "1.0.0"
date-released: 2026-09-14

repository-code: "https://github.com/LeoTorreblanca/GEO-Hubble-Geometric-Projection"

abstract: >
  Reproducible mathematical and computational audit of the GEO Hubble
  geometric-projection mapping. The repository verifies the corrected
  radial law R = mu_eff^(1/3), the canonical 45-degree membrane projection,
  the independence of the radial and projection sectors, and the closed-form
  projection factor P_GEO = sqrt(6/5). The mapping from an external Hubble
  baseline to a projected Hubble value is explicitly treated as a physical
  application hypothesis rather than as a consequence established solely
  by the software tests.

keywords:
  - "GEO"
  - "hidden geometry"
  - "Hubble tension"
  - "projection geometry"
  - "cosmology"
  - "reproducibility"

license: "MIT"
